#! ia 1.0

@cardinality one
  meaning
    says "At most one distinct target; a must obligation also requires its presence."
    answers "Is the row limited to at most one distinct target?"
  data
    order 0

@cardinality one-or-more
  meaning
    says "No upper bound; a must obligation requires at least one distinct target."
    answers "May the row have several distinct targets?"
  data
    order 1

@cardinality optional
  meaning
    says "A compatibility spelling for zero or one distinct target, including when the schema row uses must. Prefer may with one for new zero-or-one rows; both optional spellings remain admitted."
    answers "Does this existing row allow zero or one target, even when it says must?"
  data
    order 2

